{
 "about": "The Ghidra compatibility corpus (run.py): 30 of Ghidra 12.1.4's bundled scripts, ported to Python 3 in scripts/ with their API calls unchanged. Addresses are symbolic ('main', 'main+0x4', 'block:.data', '0x104010'), resolved in each program. 'args' are the script's arguments (getScriptArgs(); they answer ask* in order, as in Ghidra's headless mode; {out} is a file the script may write). 'setup' runs first on both sides; 'compare' names what must agree; 'expect' is 'agree' or {'unsupported': API}. Lines naming an address outside the memory both programs have (Ghidra's ELF EXTERNAL pseudo block, its non-loaded '.symtab::' spaces) are left out of every comparison. 'extra' scenarios are run and reported but are not among the 30. Every scenario runs on the SDK fixture (tests/fixtures/script_target.c, compiled with cc -O1) and on the corpus program elf-x86_64/gcc-O0/debug/features (corpus/manifest.json pins it); 'on' overrides a scenario's addresses and arguments per program.",
 "scenarios": [
  {
   "name": "HelloWorldScript",
   "script": "HelloWorldScript.py",
   "source": "Features/Base",
   "compare": [
    "output"
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "HelloWorldPopupScript",
   "script": "HelloWorldPopupScript.py",
   "source": "Features/Base",
   "compare": [
    "output",
    "messages"
   ]
  },
