   "why": "lists every defined data item: Ghidra's ELF loader defines the ELF headers, .dynamic, .eh_frame and symbol-sized arrays revkit's loader doesn't"
  },
  {
   "name": "IterateInstructionsScript",
   "script": "IterateInstructionsScript.py",
   "source": "Features/Base",
   "compare": [
    "output"
   ],
   "model_difference": "revkit's analysis doesn't disassemble the .plt's lazy-binding code that only the GOT reaches (the fixture's three PUSH/JMP stubs, the PUSH/JMP after each of features' PLT jumps); Ghidra's does. Every other instruction's text agrees."
  },
  {
   "name": "IterateFunctionsScript",
   "script": "IterateFunctionsScript.py",
   "source": "Features/Base",
   "args": [
    "true"
   ],
   "compare": [
    "output"
   ],
   "normalize": {
    "drop_lines": [
     "^found forward = "
    ]
   },
   "why_normalize": "Ghidra's count includes the 8 functions of its ELF EXTERNAL pseudo block, which revkit doesn't have; every function listed in the program's memory is compared"
  },
